WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.137
In lecture one

2
00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:07.601
a matrix times a vector combined columns.

3
00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:10.900
Today we multiply a matrix by a matrix.

4
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:15.058
Here is A, with two rows and three columns

5
00:00:15.058 --> 00:00:18.600
and B, with three rows and two columns.

6
00:00:18.688 --> 00:00:20.990
The three columns of A are

7
00:00:21.079 --> 00:00:22.850
arrows in the plane.

8
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.679
Before any rule: the entry in row two

9
00:00:27.679 --> 00:00:29.918
column one of A B.

10
00:00:29.918 --> 00:00:34.396
Which numbers of A and B does it use?

11
00:00:34.396 --> 00:00:36.400
Pause and guess.

12
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.764
First, the shapes.

13
00:00:41.764 --> 00:00:45.925
A is two by three, and B is three by two.

14
00:00:45.925 --> 00:00:48.601
The product is two by two

15
00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:53.060
it keeps the rows of A and the columns of B.

16
00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.875
The inner sizes must match

17
00:00:55.875 --> 00:00:59.710
A has three columns and B has three rows.

18
00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:03.635
B A also exists, but it is three by three

19
00:01:03.635 --> 00:01:05.370
a different shape.

20
00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:08.604
Way one: entry by entry.

21
00:01:08.604 --> 00:01:11.037
The entry in row two

22
00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:15.129
column one uses row two of A: three

23
00:01:15.129 --> 00:01:16.898
minus one, two.

24
00:01:16.898 --> 00:01:20.990
And column one of B: two, zero, one.

25
00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:25.795
Three times two, plus minus one times zero

26
00:01:25.795 --> 00:01:28.904
plus two times one, is eight.

27
00:01:28.904 --> 00:01:32.012
Do that for all four entries

28
00:01:32.012 --> 00:01:36.260
and A B is two, seven, eight, minus two.

29
00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.876
Way two: by columns.

30
00:01:38.978 --> 00:01:41.829
Column one of A B is A times

31
00:01:41.931 --> 00:01:45.189
column one of B: two, zero, one.

32
00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:49.771
By lecture one, that mixes the columns of A

33
00:01:49.771 --> 00:01:53.640
two of the first, none of the second

34
00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.880
and one of the third.

35
00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:59.900
Tip to tail, they land on two, eight

36
00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:02.380
the first column of A B.

37
00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:06.347
So every column of A B is a combination

38
00:02:06.446 --> 00:02:08.430
of the columns of A.

39
00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:10.937
Way three: by rows.

40
00:02:10.937 --> 00:02:15.195
Row one of A B is row one of A, one, two

41
00:02:15.195 --> 00:02:16.716
zero, times B.

42
00:02:16.716 --> 00:02:19.352
That mixes the rows of B

43
00:02:19.352 --> 00:02:21.583
one of the first row

44
00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:24.017
plus two of the second

45
00:02:24.017 --> 00:02:26.450
plus none of the third.

46
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:31.195
One of two, one, plus two of zero, three

47
00:02:31.195 --> 00:02:35.161
lands on two, seven: row one of A B.

48
00:02:35.161 --> 00:02:39.663
That is how elimination worked last time

49
00:02:39.663 --> 00:02:43.200
a matrix on the left mixes rows.

50
00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.225
Way four is the surprising one.

51
00:02:47.225 --> 00:02:51.891
Multiply column one of A by row one of B.

52
00:02:51.891 --> 00:02:56.891
A column times a row is a whole matrix: two

53
00:02:56.891 --> 00:02:58.780
one, six, three.

54
00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:02.186
Do the same with column two and row two

55
00:03:02.186 --> 00:03:05.012
and with column three and row three.

56
00:03:05.012 --> 00:03:08.450
Add the three pieces, and you get A B again.

57
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.291
Now look at the first piece in the plane.

58
00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:15.526
Its columns, two, six and one, three

59
00:03:15.526 --> 00:03:16.974
lie on one line.

60
00:03:16.974 --> 00:03:20.550
Every column is a multiple of one column

61
00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.360
so the piece is called rank one.

62
00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:26.680
A product is a sum of rank one pieces.

63
00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.293
Careful with the order.

64
00:03:29.293 --> 00:03:32.652
A column times a row is not a number.

65
00:03:32.652 --> 00:03:36.099
Column one, three, times row two, one

66
00:03:36.099 --> 00:03:38.220
is a two by two matrix.

67
00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.883
Row two, one, times column one, three

68
00:03:41.883 --> 00:03:43.626
is the number five.

69
00:03:43.626 --> 00:03:46.241
Same numbers, opposite order

70
00:03:46.241 --> 00:03:47.810
different shapes.

71
00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:52.560
Order matters even for square matrices.

72
00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.516
Take two shears: G pushes points up

73
00:03:56.516 --> 00:03:59.510
and F pushes them sideways.

74
00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.345
F G means G acts first, and then F.

75
00:04:03.345 --> 00:04:07.428
The unit square ends with columns three

76
00:04:07.428 --> 00:04:09.220
two and one, one.

77
00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:13.746
Now the other order: F first, and then G.

78
00:04:13.746 --> 00:04:17.005
The square ends somewhere else

79
00:04:17.005 --> 00:04:20.875
with columns one, two and one, three.

80
00:04:20.875 --> 00:04:22.810
So F G is not G F.

81
00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.179
What does not matter is the grouping.

82
00:04:27.179 --> 00:04:31.416
A B, then times C, equals A times B C

83
00:04:31.416 --> 00:04:34.240
so we simply write A B C.

84
00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.894
The grouping rule matters

85
00:04:36.977 --> 00:04:38.637
for neural networks.

86
00:04:38.637 --> 00:04:40.628
The first layer, W one

87
00:04:40.628 --> 00:04:44.030
takes three inputs to two hidden values.

88
00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.104
The second layer, W two

89
00:04:46.104 --> 00:04:49.340
takes those two values to two outputs.

90
00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:53.014
Feed in x equal to one, one, one.

91
00:04:53.014 --> 00:04:56.539
The hidden values are three, four.

92
00:04:56.539 --> 00:05:00.467
Then W two mixes its own columns, one

93
00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:02.884
two and one, minus one.

94
00:05:02.985 --> 00:05:06.107
Three of the first plus four of

95
00:05:06.208 --> 00:05:09.330
the second lands on seven, two.

96
00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:13.544
The single matrix W two W one gives seven

97
00:05:13.544 --> 00:05:14.832
two directly.

98
00:05:14.832 --> 00:05:18.512
Two linear layers are one linear layer.

99
00:05:18.604 --> 00:05:21.916
That is why networks put a nonlinear

100
00:05:22.008 --> 00:05:24.400
step between their layers.

101
00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:28.219
So, four views of one product.

102
00:05:28.219 --> 00:05:32.106
Each entry is a row times a column.

103
00:05:32.106 --> 00:05:36.749
Each column of A B mixes the columns of A

104
00:05:36.749 --> 00:05:40.420
and each row mixes the rows of B.

105
00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.438
The whole product is a sum of

106
00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:47.394
column times row pieces, each of rank one.

107
00:05:47.394 --> 00:05:50.430
And order matters: B acts first

108
00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.730
so it sits on the right.

109
00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.461
In part two we undo a matrix

110
00:05:56.461 --> 00:05:58.560
with its inverse.
